the biggest mistake of your life.

490
00:35:20.994 --> 00:35:24.540
I swear to God. Please. I want you
to think clearly about this.

491
00:35:25.123 --> 00:35:27.709
I'm thinking clearly. Very clearly.

492
00:35:27.793 --> 00:35:28.710
So am I.

493
00:35:30.003 --> 00:35:35.801
I really. really feel that Mom would
want us both to be here together.

494
00:35:35.884 --> 00:35:38.262
Really? Do you? You really think that?

495
00:35:38.345 --> 00:35:41.139
Or do you maybe think
the way that I think?

496
00:35:41.223 --> 00:35:45.310
Which is. I'm kind of discovering
that my life is fucking. like.

497
00:35:46.478 --> 00:35:49.606
bullshit. and I wanna see something new.

498
00:35:49.690 --> 00:35:54.653
But now I'm stuck here
because you don't want to sell?

499
00:35:56.446 --> 00:35:58.448
I can't. I can't. I'm sorry.

500
00:36:00.909 --> 00:36:03.620
Right. Right. Right.

501
00:36:09.376 --> 00:36:11.169
Ramona. I'm leaving today…

502
00:36:13.380 --> 00:36:14.381
[door slams]

503
00:36:18.886 --> 00:36:21.597
[cell phone ringing]

504
00:36:24.266 --> 00:36:25.309
Hello?

505
00:36:25.392 --> 00:36:27.519
[female voice]
<i>Hi. Is this Connor Jacobson?</i>

506
00:36:27.811 --> 00:36:29.021
Yeah.

507
00:36:29.104 --> 00:36:32.441
<i>Hi. Connor. This is Dawn Fisher</i>
<i>from Open Hearts Adoption Agency.</i>

508
00:36:33.108 --> 00:36:36.862
<i>We got a response from</i>
<i>your biological mother about your request.</i>

509
00:36:36.945 --> 00:36:40.032
<i>And she would love</i>
<i>to get in touch with you.</i>

510
00:36:48.123 --> 00:36:49.041
Hey. Maple.

511
00:36:49.875 --> 00:36:50.709
[Maple] Hi.

512
00:36:53.211 --> 00:36:55.964
Is she here? I wanna talk to her.

513
00:36:56.673 --> 00:36:57.716
Um.

514
00:36:57.799 --> 00:36:58.800
no.

515
00:37:00.135 --> 00:37:01.428
Know when she'll be back?

516
00:37:04.097 --> 00:37:05.849
Okay. Well. um…

517
00:37:07.643 --> 00:37:10.354
if you see her. let her know
I'm stuck here forever.

518
00:37:10.854 --> 00:37:12.522
if she ever wants to talk.

519
00:37:16.026 --> 00:37:16.860
Thanks.

520
00:37:19.613 --> 00:37:20.530
I'm sorry.

521
00:37:21.114 --> 00:37:21.949
Huh?

522
00:37:22.491 --> 00:37:23.533
Sorry.

523
00:37:26.411 --> 00:37:27.287
Yeah.

524
00:37:29.247 --> 00:37:30.248
Yeah. me too.

525
00:37:48.517 --> 00:37:51.103
[Maple] You know how messed up
it is to ask a child to lie?

526
00:37:51.186 --> 00:37:52.187
Yeah. I know.

527
00:37:53.021 --> 00:37:54.815
I'm sorry. And thank you.

528
00:37:58.652 --> 00:38:00.404
Why didn't you want to talk to her?

529
00:38:02.239 --> 00:38:05.075
If she knew that I was here.
she wouldn't do what she needs to do.

530
00:38:06.493 --> 00:38:09.371
Well. what does she need to do?

531
00:38:12.165 --> 00:38:14.001
She needs to do what's best for her.

532
00:38:18.171 --> 00:38:19.047
Are you okay?

533
00:38:19.131 --> 00:38:20.090
Yeah.

534
00:38:21.842 --> 00:38:22.676
Yeah.

535
00:38:23.552 --> 00:38:26.013
-Are you sure?
-Yeah. I'm good.

536
00:38:38.734 --> 00:38:39.568
Hi.

537
00:38:39.651 --> 00:38:40.652
Hey.

538
00:38:41.778 --> 00:38:44.865
I think Ellis is out there
getting the plane ready for you.

539
00:38:47.784 --> 00:38:49.578
-Okay. Thank you. Cool.
-He should be back soon.

540
00:38:49.661 --> 00:38:50.495
Cool.

541
00:39:04.134 --> 00:39:06.053
I had a dream about my mom last night.

542
00:39:11.433 --> 00:39:12.434
Yeah?

543
00:39:13.935 --> 00:39:15.812
You think she regretted
blowing up her life?

544
00:39:18.148 --> 00:39:22.736
No. I think maybe she would've done things
a little bit differently. but no.

545
00:39:27.324 --> 00:39:28.492
She was…

546
00:39:30.077 --> 00:39:31.703
She was finally happy.

547
00:39:32.746 --> 00:39:36.083
In fact. she told me
that she wished she had done it sooner.

548
00:39:42.297 --> 00:39:45.884
So what happened between
when my dad took us and when my mom died?

549
00:39:47.344 --> 00:39:50.430
-Was she gonna come back ever?
-Of course she was comin' back.

550
00:39:52.057 --> 00:39:55.685
She had a ticket to New York
two days after you left.

551
00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:57.938
Soonest one she could get.

552
00:39:58.021 --> 00:39:59.356
-Really?
-Yeah.

553
00:40:00.232 --> 00:40:02.067
So then was it the stress
of my dad taking us

554
00:40:02.150 --> 00:40:04.277
that caused her to go
into an early labor or--

555
00:40:04.361 --> 00:40:05.195
No.

556
00:40:05.779 --> 00:40:08.031
-Well. how could it not have been?
-No. no. no. [sighs]

557
00:40:10.325 --> 00:40:11.827
The doctor said no.

558
00:40:12.828 --> 00:40:13.662
Okay?

559
00:40:15.831 --> 00:40:17.165
She had a heart condition.

560
00:40:19.709 --> 00:40:20.961
I mean. nobody knew.

561
00:40:23.421 --> 00:40:27.801
So. like…
what exactly happened that night?

562
00:40:27.884 --> 00:40:28.969
[sighing] Annie. uh…

563
00:40:30.595 --> 00:40:31.429
I'm sorry. I…

564
00:40:32.639 --> 00:40:33.473
Okay.

565
00:40:35.934 --> 00:40:37.269
She was…

566
00:40:38.520 --> 00:40:39.479
She was in pain.

567
00:40:41.314 --> 00:40:46.945
And she didn't know if it was contractions
or not. you know. so…

568
00:40:48.071 --> 00:40:49.531
I rushed her to the hospital.

569
00:40:51.449 --> 00:40:52.951
I remember thinking that…

570
00:40:54.911 --> 00:40:58.039
There was no way this boat
could move slower. you know.

571
00:40:58.123 --> 00:41:00.458
but we were flying across the lake.

572
00:41:01.710 --> 00:41:03.086
I kept pushing it.

573
00:41:03.170 --> 00:41:06.214
I actually bent the throttle.

574
00:41:08.633 --> 00:41:09.759
And we got there.

575
00:41:09.843 --> 00:41:14.347
And I just remember
all these doctors and nurses.

576
00:41:14.973 --> 00:41:15.932
It was packed.

577
00:41:16.016 --> 00:41:18.476
And I kept getting pushed out.

578
00:41:18.560 --> 00:41:20.687
And so I was standing in the doorway.

579
00:41:21.813 --> 00:41:23.190
and I heard this crash.

580
00:41:23.815 --> 00:41:25.442
I remember I looked down the hall.

581
00:41:26.818 --> 00:41:29.946
and this doctor.
he was older than everyone else.

582
00:41:30.739 --> 00:41:32.991
came flyin' around the corner.

583
00:41:33.617 --> 00:41:37.621
and he ran into this medical cart.
and shit went flyin' everywhere.

584
00:41:38.205 --> 00:41:40.832
And he sprinted
right past me into the room.

585
00:41:42.042 --> 00:41:44.669
and I remember that
that is when it dawned on me

586
00:41:44.753 --> 00:41:47.130
that this was bad. you know?

587
00:41:49.841 --> 00:41:52.219
And they. uh. took her into surgery.

588
00:41:52.302 --> 00:41:56.139
Surgery? What s… What sur…
I didn't know she had surgery.

589
00:41:56.223 --> 00:41:58.558
She had an emergency C-section.

590
00:41:58.642 --> 00:42:00.101
I didn't know she had a C-section.

591
00:42:02.395 --> 00:42:03.688
[sighs]

592
00:42:05.732 --> 00:42:07.067
Was she… Was she scared?

593
00:42:10.946 --> 00:42:12.364
You know. your mom.

594
00:42:13.823 --> 00:42:17.285
she was the bravest. most fearless person

595
00:42:18.328 --> 00:42:20.038
I had ever known.

596
00:42:20.872 --> 00:42:24.209
And when they were taking her
out of the room. we made eye contact.

597
00:42:25.919 --> 00:42:27.921
and I remember she smiled at me.

598
00:42:28.964 --> 00:42:32.884
you know. like she was gonna reassure me.
[chuckles sadly]

599
00:42:41.017 --> 00:42:42.018
And then what happened?

600
00:42:42.102 --> 00:42:44.104
Well. then I never saw her again.

601
00:42:44.980 --> 00:42:46.398
She didn't come out of surgery.

602
00:42:50.235 --> 00:42:52.070
So she never got to meet Ramona?

603
00:42:53.655 --> 00:42:55.282
Or hold her? Anything like that?

604
00:42:59.661 --> 00:43:00.495
No.

605
00:43:04.499 --> 00:43:05.333
No.

606
00:43:11.923 --> 00:43:13.925
["Don't Think Twice.
It's Alright" playing]

607
00:43:58.970 --> 00:43:59.888
Hi.

608
00:44:01.514 --> 00:44:03.099
I'm so glad you're here. I was…

609
00:44:03.725 --> 00:44:07.228
You know. I was hoping
I could… see you before I left.

610
00:44:07.812 --> 00:44:08.646
-Um…
-Yeah.

611
00:44:10.231 --> 00:44:13.485
I don't know where your head is or if…

612
00:44:14.486 --> 00:44:16.029
there's a world where maybe…

613
00:44:17.572 --> 00:44:20.909
you and I could spend some time together.
'Cause I really wanna…

614
00:44:24.788 --> 00:44:26.915
[sentimental music playing]

615
00:44:50.939 --> 00:44:52.107
Ramona?

616
00:44:53.024 --> 00:44:55.068
You've been girl
with dead mom your whole life.

617
00:44:56.903 --> 00:44:57.779
Okay.

618
00:44:57.862 --> 00:44:59.656
And you've always had this place and her…

619
00:45:00.407 --> 00:45:03.451
all of her memories
and Gordon and… I mean…

620
00:45:03.535 --> 00:45:05.703
You slept in her bed every summer.
Like. that's…

621
00:45:07.831 --> 00:45:09.207
That's so incredible.

622
00:45:10.291 --> 00:45:11.292
I want that.

623
00:45:12.085 --> 00:45:13.962
I need to be girl with dead mom too.

624
00:45:15.171 --> 00:45:17.465
And you've never gotten
to be girl with an alive dad.

625
00:45:18.091 --> 00:45:19.217
And I have had that.

626
00:45:21.010 --> 00:45:23.012
For 18 years. I've had that.

627
00:45:25.515 --> 00:45:27.100
Ho…

628
00:45:28.017 --> 00:45:29.936
And honestly. he's a really good dad.

629
00:45:31.604 --> 00:45:33.064
And I want you to have that.

630
00:45:33.148 --> 00:45:35.859
And I really do want you to have that.

631
00:45:37.861 --> 00:45:40.196
["Fleeting" playing]

632
00:45:49.956 --> 00:45:51.666
You deserve to be taken care of.

633
00:45:52.542 --> 00:45:54.169
Yeah. No. I know I deserve that.

634
00:45:56.713 --> 00:45:58.715
I just… I don't know if I want it.

635
00:46:01.676 --> 00:46:02.552
Well. I think…

636
00:46:04.220 --> 00:46:05.305
I think you need it.

637
00:46:07.891 --> 00:46:09.142
How do you know what I need?

638
00:46:15.190 --> 00:46:16.399
Because I'm your sister.

639
00:46:26.784 --> 00:46:28.203
[Ramona] <i>So what should we do?</i>

640
00:47:56.874 --> 00:48:00.295
[slow instrumental music playing]

641
00:48:01.305 --> 00:49:01.882
